 solar power from both owned generation facilities and PPAs, as well as its fossil fuel energy portfolio, such as coal and natural gas; sale and resale of wholesale transmission service; and engages in wholesale commodity and trading operations. It also purchases, transports, stores, distributes, and sells natural gas; develops and leases natural gas pipelines and storage facilities; operates interstate natural gas pipeline; and invests in rental housing projects, energy technology companies, and community solar garden nonregulated assets. It serves electric and natural gas customers in portions of Colorado, Michigan, Minnesota, New Mexico, North Dakota, South Dakota, Texas, and Wisconsin. The company was formerly known as Northern States Power company. Xcel Energy Inc. was incorporated in 1909 and is headquartered in Minneapolis, Minnesota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert C. Frenzel | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 54 | Compensation: $4.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 11K people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the above the sector median among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Xcel Energy Inc. is a large-cap utilities business with a $50.9B market cap on $14.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $6.8B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, 